    Mailbox answers require an explicit marker, not a filename substring
    
    Rebuild of dbdfbb7 onto current main 297233f. A report is pending unless an
    explicit empty sibling marker '<report>.md.answered' (or '.disposition')
    exists; the filename substring no longer suppresses the signal.

diff --git a/government/AGENT-REPORTING-POLICY.md b/government/AGENT-REPORTING-POLICY.md
index 82b380d6..cccdba78 100644
--- a/government/AGENT-REPORTING-POLICY.md
+++ b/government/AGENT-REPORTING-POLICY.md
@@ -28,6 +28,13 @@ Every Town agent receives this instruction at startup and resumption:
   misconduct or of a particular cause. Never convert "unknown", successful
   agent exits or readiness into verified completion. Verify the monitoring
   system itself.
+- An answer to a mailbox report is recorded by an explicit, empty sibling
+  marker beside the report: `<report>.md.answered` (or `<report>.md.disposition`).
+  A report is counted as pending unless that marker exists. A bare
+  `addendum` or `disposition` substring in a report's own filename no longer
+  suppresses the pending signal, so a genuine blocker cannot be hidden by
+  choosing such a name. Writing an addendum file in addition to the marker is
+  encouraged, but the marker is the machine-readable answer.
 
 For Judiciary reviewers: reporting is NOT review. A disposition may say
 "independently verified" only after identifying the evidence inspected
diff --git a/government/branch-health.sh b/government/branch-health.sh
index fec8231e..0ceba888 100755
--- a/government/branch-health.sh
+++ b/government/branch-health.sh
@@ -85,19 +85,19 @@ for observation in "outcomes:$state/institutional-outcomes/latest.json" "institu
   fi
 done
 # Unreviewed agent impediments are unresolved adverse evidence. A reviewer's
-# own disposition or addendum is an answer, not a pending question, and must
-# not hold the signal red forever. This is a deterministic filename convention
-# because the mailbox has no metadata sidecar; it does not remove or rewrite
-# any preserved report.
+# answer is recorded by an explicit marker file beside the report, never by a
+# substring of the report's own filename: a reporter must not be able to
+# suppress a genuine blocker by choosing a name that happens to contain
+# "addendum" or "disposition". The marker is empty and additive; it does not
+# remove or rewrite any preserved report.
 mailbox_dir="$state/oversight/judiciary-mailbox/inbox"
 pending_mailbox=no
 if [ -d "$mailbox_dir" ]; then
   for mailbox_file in "$mailbox_dir"/*.md; do
     [ -f "$mailbox_file" ] || continue
-    mailbox_name=$(basename "$mailbox_file")
-    case "$mailbox_name" in
-      *disposition*|*addendum*) continue ;;
-    esac
+    if [ -f "$mailbox_file.answered" ] || [ -f "$mailbox_file.disposition" ]; then
+      continue
+    fi
     pending_mailbox=yes
     break
   done
